    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0430" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.91293/7–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-11T13:00:00+08:00">July 11, 1949—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 11—7:57 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 709. Re Generalissimo’s press interview from Formosa, reliably informed by
                    other American correspondents who also sought interview unsuccessfully that
                    apparently special considerations resulted <pb facs="0431" n="421"
                        xml:id="pg421"/> choice INS<anchor n="82" xml:id="d489-f1"/> Handelman and
                    Scripps-Howard Farnsworth. Handelman came specially from Tokyo to attend. Others
                    had been turned down only few days before grounds Generalissimo in retirement.
                    Seems possible suggestion originated Stateside, possibly Madame,<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d489-f2"/> for interview with attention paid propaganda value there
                    in China aid cause.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d489-f1" n="82" xml:id="d489-f1-content">
